# Level 37, reached by password, then a spin fight against $81:E6E4 -- the one
# address the decline census had on it.
#
# **The census named an address and the address named a level, in that order,
# which is how this is supposed to go.** `movies/level29-ice.zmv` reached
# `$81:E6E4` exactly **once**, which is enough to name a routine and not enough
# to write one against: one call cannot reach more than one of eight branches.
# So the input came first.
#
# Finding the level took three ROM reads and no play at all:
#
#   1. `A9 E4 E6` -- LDA #$E6E4 -- occurs once in the ROM, at `$81:E476`, inside
#      the actor init `$81:E413`, which also seeds this creature's health to 3.
#   2. Two behaviours `JSR $E413`: `$81:E481` and `$81:E51A`. Every other copy of
#      `$81:8888` belongs to one behaviour; this one is shared, which is why it
#      turns up on nine levels with nine different actor types in front of it.
#   3. Of the levels a password reaches, 29, 33 and 37 place one. Level 29's is
#      inside solid scenery, all seven of level 33's are cut off from its spawn,
#      and **level 37's `$81:E481` at (1057,204) is 61 cells from the spawn**.
#
# `zamn_assets route ... --reach` is what says "inside scenery" rather than
# "far", and it is also what caught a bug while doing it: level 33's actor list
# places one at (1260,1737) on a level 1280 pixels tall, and the route search had
# been indexing `prev` with an off-map goal and answering out of whatever was
# past the end of the array. It range-checks both ends now.
#
# The route is **two legs** and the fitter found them first try. The fight is a
# spin -- 30-frame legs, four directions, Y held -- rather than a stand, because
# four of these things crowd the player at once from three sides, and the same
# tap-and-turn shape that `movies/level21-spin.zmv` established is what faces
# all of them in turn.
#
# What it buys: **367 calls to `$81:E6E4`, against the one call that named it.**
# `e6e4_ignore` 1720, `e6e4_hit` 46, `e6e4_died` 46 -- and the two deaths watched
# frame by frame both carry `$22` = `$0060`, damage 4 against health 3, which is
# `$0003 -> $FFFF` in one hit. It is not the player's weapon: `$7E:1CBC` is
# parked at `$0012` by a pickup from 2980 to 4158 and reads 0 after, so the
# player's own shots are `$5C`. Something else on this level lands them.
#
